# wallet_carver

Forensic recovery tool for Bitcoin/Electrum key material from a raw `dd`/`ddrescue`
image — **even when the filesystem is destroyed/overwritten**.

> **Focus:** this tool works exclusively on **raw `dd`/`ddrescue` images** and reads the
> **byte stream directly** — no filesystem, no mounting, no wallet software. That means it
> recovers key material even when the filesystem is **destroyed, overwritten, or only
> partially rescued with `ddrescue`**. It is meant for recovering **your own** wallets, runs
> **offline**, and reports **only structurally validated hits** (no false positives).

---

## What it finds

| Scheme | Content |
|---|---|
| `wif` | WIF private keys (base58check) |
| `ext` | Extended keys `xprv`/`xpub`/`tprv`/`tpub` |
| `electrum-v4` | Pre-2.0 Electrum wallet (`seed_version 4`, 2011–2014) — incl. password testing |
| `electrum-2x-plain` | Electrum 2.x wallet in plaintext (JSON) |
| `electrum-bie1` | Electrum 2.x encrypted wallet (`BIE1`/ECIES) — incl. password testing |
| `core-mkey` | Bitcoin Core `wallet.dat` (`mkey`/`ckey`) — incl. password testing |
| `mnemonic-file` | Standalone file whose **entire** content is ONLY a seed (BIP39 or any Electrum type) |
| `bip39` | BIP39 seed embedded anywhere in larger text (sliding window) |
| `hex` | raw 64-hex private-key candidates (**unverified**, not in `all`) |

Electrum seed types detected: **old** (1.x, hex + optional old mnemonic) and **new** (2.0+):
`standard` (0x01), `segwit` (0x100), `2fa` (0x101), `2fa_segwit` (0x102).

---

## Installation (Ubuntu)

Recommended: a dedicated **virtualenv**, so nothing touches the system Python.

```bash
# 1) system packages
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y python3 python3-venv python3-pip

# 2) create and activate a virtualenv
python3 -m venv ~/wallet-carver-venv
source ~/wallet-carver-venv/bin/activate

# 3) install dependencies
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install cryptography mnemonic
```

- **`cryptography`** — required (AES-CBC for all decryptions).
- **`mnemonic`** — only for BIP39 (checksum validation). Without it, every other scheme still
  runs; only BIP39 is skipped. Electrum seeds do **not** need it.
- **optional `electrum`** (`pip install electrum`) — automatically enables detection of
  **standalone old Electrum mnemonics** (needs the 1626-word list). Alternatively pass
  `--electrum-old-wordlist <file>`.

Then place the script in your project directory and run it (venv active):

```bash
python wallet_carver.py --selftest     # verifies all crypto primitives, must print "PASS"
```

> If you use a specific interpreter (e.g. `python3.14`), create the venv with it:
> `python3.14 -m venv ~/wallet-carver-venv`.

**Alternative without a venv:** `python3 wallet_carver.py --install-deps -i …` installs the
packages itself (on Ubuntu's "externally-managed-environment" it automatically falls back to
`--break-system-packages`). A venv is cleaner, though.

---

## Creating the image (dd / ddrescue)

The tool reads an **image file**, not a live drive. Create it from the source device first
(and **never** write to the source drive). `ddrescue` is more robust with bad sectors and can
resume thanks to its mapfile:

```bash
# preferred: ddrescue (skips read errors, mapfile allows resuming)
sudo apt install -y gddrescue
sudo ddrescue -d -r3 /dev/sdX disk.img disk.mapfile

# simple alternative with dd
sudo dd if=/dev/sdX of=disk.img bs=4M conv=noerror,sync status=progress
```

Replace `/dev/sdX` with the **source drive**. Afterwards the tool works exclusively on
`disk.img` — the original stays untouched. Incomplete `ddrescue` images (with gaps from
unreadable sectors) are usable too: the raw byte stream is what gets scanned.

---

## Quick start

```bash
# just view the scheme list
python wallet_carver.py --list-schemes

# search the whole image, test passwords, check balances
python wallet_carver.py \
  -i /path/to/disk.img \
  -p password_list.txt \
  -s '*' \
  --check-balance \
  -o carver.out
```

- `password_list.txt`: one password per line (UTF-8). Encrypted candidates are tested against
  **every** password.
- Output: `carver.out/findings.jsonl` (mode `0600`, written **live** per hit). Every valid hit
  is also shown **immediately** on screen.

### "Find everything" — one command

```bash
python wallet_carver.py -i disk.img -p password_list.txt -s '*' --check-balance -o carver.out
```

`-s '*'` enables every detector (including the unverified `hex`). `-s all` is identical but
omits `hex` (recommended if you only want validated hits).

---

## Scheme selection (`-s` / `--schemes`)

Comma list of: exact id · wildcard · group · `all` · `*`

```bash
-s all                     # all validated schemes (without hex)
-s '*'                     # literally everything (incl. hex)
-s 'electrum-*'            # all Electrum schemes
-s electrum-v4,core-mkey   # just these two
-s mnemonic-file           # standalone seed files only
```

---

## Key options

| Option | Effect |
|---|---|
| `-i FILE` | raw image (`dd`/`ddrescue`) — **required** |
| `-p FILE` | password list (one per line) |
| `-o DIR` | output directory (default `./carver_out`) |
| `-s LIST` | scheme selection (default `all`) |
| `--check-balance` | derive addresses **and** query on-chain balance |
| `--addresses-only` | derive addresses, **no** API query (OPSEC-safe) |
| `--api-url URL` | Esplora-compatible API (default `https://blockstream.info/api`) |
| `--gap N` | gap limit for seed/xprv derivation (default 20) |
| `--hex` | additionally run the `hex` scheme (unverified) |
| `--seedfile-nochecksum` | `mnemonic-file`: also report exact 12/24-word regions with a **failing** checksum |
| `--electrum-old-wordlist FILE` | 1626-word list for old Electrum mnemonics |
| `--min-iter N` / `--max-iter N` | sanity window for Core `mkey` iterations |
| `--no-progress` | disable the progress bar |
| `--install-deps` | install packages via pip |
| `--list-schemes` | show available schemes |
| `--selftest` | verify crypto primitives against test vectors |

---

## Checking balances & privacy

```bash
# OPSEC-safe: derive addresses only, check them yourself on your own node
python wallet_carver.py -i disk.img -s all --addresses-only -o out
#   -> out/addresses.txt

# with a query (discloses your addresses to the API server!)
python wallet_carver.py -i disk.img -s all --check-balance -o out
#   -> out/balances.txt  (hits shown live on screen, ">>>" = has a balance)
```

> **Privacy note:** `--check-balance` discloses the queried addresses to the API operator. For
> maximum privacy use `--addresses-only` + your own node, or
> `--api-url https://<your-esplora-instance>/api` (e.g. mempool.space-compatible).

Addresses derived per hit type:
- Private keys → P2PKH (compressed/uncompressed), P2WPKH, P2SH-P2WPKH
- Old Electrum seed → its own derivation (uncompressed P2PKH)
- Electrum new → `standard` (m/0,m/1 P2PKH) or `segwit` (m/0' P2WPKH); 2FA reported only
- xprv/xpub/BIP39 → BIP44/49/84 + Electrum paths (common paths, gap limit)

---

## Output files (`-o`)

| File | Content |
|---|---|
| `findings.jsonl` | one JSON object per hit, written live, mode `0600` |
| `addresses.txt` | derived addresses (with `--check-balance`/`--addresses-only`) |
| `balances.txt` | used/funded addresses with balance (with `--check-balance`) |

`status` values: `VALID` / `DECRYPTED` / `PLAINTEXT` = confirmed hit ·
`ENCRYPTED` = found but no password matched · `UNVERIFIED` = hex candidate with no guarantee.

---

## Why no false positives

Every reported hit is **structurally validated**, not just signature-matched:
- WIF/xprv: base58check (deterministic)
- Core `mkey`: the correct password yields a full PKCS7 pad block `0x10`×16 (random chance ≈ 256⁻¹⁶)
- Electrum `BIE1`: the HMAC-SHA256 over the ECIES blob **is** the password check
- Old Electrum seed: decrypts to exactly 32 hex chars (PKCS7-checked)
- BIP39: valid checksum; `mnemonic-file` additionally requires "the region contains ONLY the seed"
- Electrum new: canonical `HMAC("Seed version")` version prefix

Exception: `hex` (raw 64-hex keys) cannot be structurally validated → off by default, marked
`UNVERIFIED`.

---

## Troubleshooting

- **`externally-managed-environment` on pip install** → use a venv (above), or `--install-deps`
  (automatically falls back to `--break-system-packages`).
- **`SyntaxError` on startup** → run the script with **python** (`python wallet_carver.py …`),
  not with `bash`.
- **Image is a block device instead of a file** → copy it to a file with `dd` first (the tool
  uses `mmap`; for devices it falls back to a full read and needs RAM ≥ image size).
- **API 403 / rate limiting** → your own Esplora node via `--api-url`, or `--addresses-only`.
- **BIP39 is skipped** → `pip install mnemonic` (Electrum seeds don't need it).
- Large images: the progress bar shows %, MB/s, ETA; multiple passes are chunked (64 MiB with
  overlap), and hits straddling chunk boundaries are not lost.

